.(SCOPA

  HOW TO PLAY

  Scopa is an Italian card game for two players. You capture cards from the
  table by matching their values, and score points for what you capture.
  The first player to reach 11 points wins.

  The cards
    Use a normal deck with the 8s, 9s and 10s taken out, leaving 40 cards.
    Each card is worth its number. Aces are worth 1, Jacks 8, Queens 9 and
    Kings 10. Diamonds are the most valuable suit, and the 7 of diamonds
    (the "settebello", or "beautiful seven") is the most valuable card.

  Dealing
    Shuffle, then deal 3 cards to each player and 4 cards face up in the
    middle of the table. When both players have played all their cards,
    deal 3 more to each player. Nothing more goes to the middle. Keep going
    until the deck runs out. That is one hand.

  Your turn
    Play one card from your hand. Either:
    - Take: capture cards from the middle whose values add up to the value
      of your card. For example, play a 7 to take a 3 and a 4. Put the
      captured cards and your own card face down in front of you.
      If a card in the middle has the same value as yours, you must take
      that card on its own. You can't take a combination instead.
    - Drop: put your card face up in the middle. You can only do this if
      your card can't capture anything. If you can capture, you must.
    Then it's the other player's turn.

  Scopa
    If you take every card in the middle, leaving it empty, that's a
    "scopa" (a sweep) and is worth 1 point. A sweep on the very last play
    of a hand doesn't count.

  End of a hand
    When the deck is used up and both hands are empty, whoever made the last
    capture takes any cards still in the middle (this isn't a scopa). Then
    each player looks at the cards they captured, and points are scored:
    - Most cards: 1 point.
    - Most diamonds: 1 point.
    - The 7 of diamonds: 1 point to whoever has it.
    - Primiera: 1 point (see below).
    - Each scopa: 1 point.
    If players tie for most cards, most diamonds or the primiera, nobody
    gets that point.

  Primiera
    Each player picks their best card in each of the four suits, using these
    special values:
        7 = 21    6 = 18    Ace = 16    5 = 15    4 = 14
        3 = 13    2 = 12    Jack, Queen, King = 10
    and adds the four together. The higher total wins the point. You need
    at least one card in every suit to win the primiera.
    For example: best spade a 7 (21), best heart a 6 (18), best club an
    Ace (16) and best diamond a 5 (15) gives 70.

  Winning
    After each hand, if someone has 11 or more points, the player with the
    most points wins. If players are tied for the lead, play another hand.
    The deal alternates between hands, and the player who didn't deal goes
    first.)

name scopa
players 2

.(a normal deck without the 8s, 9s and 10s: 40 cards)
deck standard without Eight Nine Ten

values { Jack 8, Queen 9, King 10 }

.(the special values used for the primiera; each card gets card:primiera)
values primiera {
    Seven 21, Six 18, Ace 16, Five 15, Four 14, Three 13, Two 12
    Jack 10, Queen 10, King 10
}

stack middle
player stack collection

number dealer
number last_capturer
player number score
player number scopas


def setup(){
    dealer = 1
    new_hand()
}

def new_hand(){
    gather()
    shuffle(deck)
    last_capturer = 0
    every player p {
        p:scopas = 0
    }
    .(the player who didn't deal goes first)
    if(dealer is 1){
        current_player = 2
    } else {
        current_player = 1
    }
    deck > middle 4
    deck > players 3
}

def player_move(player, move){
    check(player:id is current_player, it's not your turn)
    valid_moves(take, drop)
    next_player()
    after_move()
}


.(Moves)

def take(player, move){
    check(count(move:cards) is 1, play one card from your hand, e.g. take 5d / 2c 3s)
    check(count(move:target) > 0, put a / before the cards you're capturing, e.g. take 5d / 2c 3s)
    check(cards_in_stack(move:cards, player:hand), you can only play a card from your hand)
    check(cards_in_stack(move:target, middle), you can only capture cards from the middle)
    check(sum(move:target) is sum(move:cards), the cards you capture must add up to the card you play)
    if(any card c in middle: c:value is sum(move:cards)){
        check(count(move:target) is 1, a card in the middle matches yours - you must take that card on its own)
    }

    middle > player:collection taking move:target
    player:hand > player:collection taking move:cards
    last_capturer = player:id

    .(clearing the middle is a scopa, unless it was the last play of the hand)
    if(count(middle) is 0 & is_last_play() is false){
        player:scopas = player:scopas + 1
    }
}

def drop(player, move){
    check(count(move:cards) is 1, drop one card, e.g. drop 5d)
    check(count(move:target) is 0, to capture cards use take, e.g. take 5d / 2c 3s)
    check(cards_in_stack(move:cards, player:hand), you can only drop a card from your hand)
    check(can_capture(player) is false, you can capture, so you must - use take)
    player:hand > middle taking move:cards
}

.(true if any card in the hand can capture: some cards in the middle add up to it)
def can_capture(player){
    return(any card c in player:hand: any group g in middle: sum(g) is c:value)
}


.(The end of a hand)

.(true once the deck and every hand are empty)
def is_last_play(){
    return(count(deck) is 0 & every player p: count(p:hand) is 0)
}

def after_move(){
    if(every player p: count(p:hand) is 0){
        if(count(deck) > 0){
            deck > players 3
        } else {
            end_hand()
        }
    }
}

def end_hand(){
    .(whoever captured last takes what's left in the middle)
    every player p {
        if(p:id is last_capturer){
            middle > p:collection end
        }
    }

    give_point(most player p: count(p:collection))
    give_point(most player p: count(filter(p:collection, is_diamond)))
    give_point(most player p: primiera(p:collection))
    every player p {
        .(the settebello)
        if(cards_in_stack([7d], p:collection)){
            p:score = p:score + 1
        }
        p:score = p:score + p:scopas
    }

    .(first to 11 wins; if tied for the lead, play another hand)
    if((any player p: p:score >= 11) & (most player p: p:score) > 0){
        winner(most player p: p:score)
        end()
    } else {
        next_hand()
    }
}

def next_hand(){
    if(dealer is 1){
        dealer = 2
    } else {
        dealer = 1
    }
    new_hand()
}


.(Scoring)

.(1 point to a player; nobody scores when id is 0, which is what most gives for a tie)
def give_point(id){
    every player p {
        if(p:id is id){
            p:score = p:score + 1
        }
    }
}

def is_diamond(card){
    return(card:suit is Diamonds)
}

.(the best card of each suit by primiera value, added up; 0 without all four suits)
def primiera(pile){
    if(has_every_suit(pile) is false){
        return(0)
    }
    return(best_in_suit(pile, Spades) + best_in_suit(pile, Hearts)
        + best_in_suit(pile, Clubs) + best_in_suit(pile, Diamonds))
}

.(the highest primiera value among the cards of one suit, or 0 if there are none)
def best_in_suit(pile, suit){
    every card c in pile {
        if(c:suit is suit & every card d in pile: d:suit is not suit or c:primiera >= d:primiera){
            return(c:primiera)
        }
    }
    return(0)
}

def has_every_suit(pile){
    return(best_in_suit(pile, Spades) > 0 & best_in_suit(pile, Hearts) > 0
        & best_in_suit(pile, Clubs) > 0 & best_in_suit(pile, Diamonds) > 0)
}
